## Repository Path Aliases

These aliases are used in discussion and Cursor navigation to refer to key areas of the repository. They do not change runtime imports unless separately configured.

- `@functions/` → [functions/src/](mdc:functions/src/)
  - Cloud Functions TypeScript source directory

- `@public/` → [public/](mdc:public/)
  - Firebase Hosting public root and Flutter web build output

- `@_flutter_clonetrip/` → [_flutter_clonetrip/](mdc:_flutter_clonetrip/)
  - Flutter application project root

### Notes
- Firebase Functions are implemented in TypeScript (Node.js).
- TypeScript compiler options for Cloud Functions are configured in [functions/tsconfig.json](mdc:functions/tsconfig.json).
- Flutter/Dart imports are managed via [_flutter_clonetrip/pubspec.yaml](mdc:_flutter_clonetrip/pubspec.yaml) and do not use these aliases.
- To build Flutter web into `public/`, run:
```bash
cd _flutter_clonetrip
flutter build web --release -o ../public
```